WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.300
Each of your kidneys holds
about a million nephrons:

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.370
its tiny working units.

3
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.910
At the start of each one, blood pressure
forces fluid out of the blood and through

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.010
a filter.

5
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:15.690
All of your blood plasma goes through
those filters about sixty times a day.

6
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.350
And yet you don't spend
the whole day drinking.

7
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.170
So where does all that filtered fluid go?

8
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.820
Why don't you run dry?

9
00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:26.030
In this mission, you'll
follow blood into one nephron,

10
00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.540
and zoom in on the filter itself.

11
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:33.260
Then you'll zoom into a tubule cell, with
its brush of microvilli and its crowd

12
00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.710
of mitochondria.

13
00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:39.220
Your mission: find out why filtering all
that plasma doesn't leave you running

14
00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:39.890
dry.
